# Kept in git, kept off the deployed site.
#
# Everything here is developer material. Without this file Vercel uploads the
# whole repo, so /HANDOFF.md and /tools/check.py were being served from the
# site root — internal notes on a clinical practice's public website, and
# crawlable, since robots.txt allows everything.
#
# The site itself references none of these, so excluding them changes nothing
# a visitor can see.

HANDOFF.md
tools/

# Developer docs and the case data (the admin API reads cases from GitHub,
# not from the deployment), so neither needs to be public.
README.md
data/
